          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fastapi",
          "user_view_type": "public"
        }
      },
      "body": "The default `websocket_request_validation_exception_handler` currently passes the result of `jsonable_encoder(exc.errors())` directly to `WebSocket.close()` as the `reason`.\r\n\r\n`jsonable_encoder(exc.errors())` returns a list, while `WebSocket.close()` expects `reason` to be a `str | None`. As a result, WebSocket request-validation errors can cause the exception handler itself to fail instead of closing the connection with the intended `1008` policy-violation code.\r\n\r\nThis change serializes the validation errors with `json.dumps()` before passing them to `WebSocket.close()`. The reason is therefore a valid string containing machine-readable JSON.\r\n\r\nA regression test was added to verify that:\r\n\r\n- WebSocket request-validation failures close with code `1008`.\r\n- The close reason is a string.\r\n- The reason contains the expected validation error.\r\n- The behavior fails with the previous implementation and passes with this fix.\r\n\r\nThe change is intentionally minimal and does not alter the validation behavior or the WebSocket close code.",
      "changed_files": 2,
      "closed_at": null,
      "comments": 0,
      "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16385/comments",
